From 494d68c0ed8e4b76d8304489f724c7f2eb98241a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Laraib Waheed <laraib.waheed@arbisoft.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:26:03 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat: extend HTTP_ALLOW_LIST to support URL rules with
 protocol/port/path matching

Entries can now optionally pin protocol, port, and path in addition to hostname, so operators can be more restrictive than a blanket hostname bypass (e.g. http://example.internal:8080/mcp, example.internal:8080/mcp, [fd00::1]:8080/mcp). Path matching uses segment boundaries so "/mcp" does not also allow "/mcp-admin". Bare hostnames retain existing behavior.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
